# GSH Builder Migration Contract

**Status:** **PENDING SIGN-OFF**  
**Decision:** DL-22  
**Phase introduced:** Portal Shell Phase 3 / Blueprint Phase 3  
**PCMS follow-up:** PCMS-003 updated in same phase (see [member-session-portal-authority.mdoc](../../standards/member-session-portal-authority.mdoc) §5.1)

This contract defines **zero-ambiguity** behavior for migrating from `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl` to `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl`. No application code in this document.

---

## 1. Scope

| Builder | Package | Status today | Target |
| ------- | ------- | ------------ | ------ |
| `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(host)` | `guest-surface-host` | **Active** — hardcodes `/me/registrations` | **Deprecated** — delegates per §4 |
| `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host, moduleId?)` | `guest-surface-host` | **Not implemented** | **Primary** from Phase 3 |

**Out of scope:** `resolvePortalRegistrationUrl`, marketing builders, web redirect shims — see [routing-builders-authority.mdoc](./routing-builders-authority.mdoc).

---

## 2. API semantics (target)

### 2.1 `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host, moduleId?)`

| Parameter | Required | Behavior |
| --------- | -------- | -------- |
| `host` | Yes | Ingress host for WRS tenant resolution (same as all GSH builders) |
| `moduleId` | No | When omitted → resolve **`defaultPrimaryModuleId`** from generated member registry for host's `pluginId` |
| `moduleId` | Yes | Resolve **route path** for that module from registry |

**Return value:** Absolute URL `{portalBase}{routePath}` where `routePath` is registry-resolved (e.g. `/me/home`, `/me/registrations`).

**Fail-closed (codegen/runtime):** Unknown `moduleId` → throw at build time (codegen) or resolve to `defaultPrimaryModuleId` at runtime (implementation detail — must be documented in GSH spec PR).

### 2.2 `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(host)` (deprecated)

**Semantic name:** “Member area entry URL for cross-host static egress (PCMS-003).”

**Not** synonymous with “default primary module” after Phase 4 — but **must remain SMK-compatible** via delegation rules in §4.

---

## 3. Fallback behaviour

Fallback chain when registry is unavailable (Phase 1–2 before codegen, or degraded SSR):

```text
resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)
  1. Generated registry → defaultPrimaryModuleId → routePath
  2. Fallback: moduleId "trips" → routePath "/me/registrations"  (URL freeze)
  3. Never throw for missing registry in GSH — use frozen alias

resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host, "trips")
  → always "{portalBase}/me/registrations"  (permanent alias — DL-03)

resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(host)  [deprecated]
  → identical to resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)  (delegation — §4)
```

**Invariant:** `{portalBase}/me/registrations` must remain reachable from both builders when `defaultPrimaryModuleId` is `home` or any other module (alias is route-level, not module-id-level).

---

## 4. Delegation (deprecated builder)

From **Phase 3 implementation** until **Cleanup Phase** (see [cleanup-roadmap.mdoc](./cleanup-roadmap.mdoc)):

```typescript
// Contract (conceptual — not implementation)
export function resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(host: string): string {
  return resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host); // delegates to defaultPrimaryModuleId
}
```

| Rule | Detail |
| ---- | ------ |
| Export preserved | `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl` **remains exported** through Cleanup Phase |
| Implementation | Single-line delegate to `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)` — no independent path logic |
| JSDoc | `@deprecated Use resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl. Removed in Cleanup Phase.` |
| Tests | Existing GSH spec expectations updated to assert delegation equivalence |

**When `defaultPrimaryModuleId` becomes `home` (Phase 4):**

| Builder | Resolves to | SMK impact |
| ------- | ----------- | ---------- |
| `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)` | `{portalBase}/me/home` | SMK-PTL-05 updated to assert `/` → `/me/home` **only when** default changes (explicit smoke PR) |
| `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(host)` | Same as above (delegates) | PCMS-003 marketing link follows default — **not** frozen to `/me/registrations` |
| Frozen alias route | `/me/registrations` still valid | SMK-PTL-02/04 **unchanged** — alias independent of default |

**PCMS-003 clarification:** Marketing “member area” egress link tracks **`defaultPrimaryModuleId`**, not the frozen alias path. The alias exists for bookmarks, workspace CTAs during migration, and SMK-PTL-02/04 — not for PCMS static egress after Phase 4.

---

## 5. Compatibility matrix

| Consumer | Phase 1–2 | Phase 3–4 | Phase 5+ | Cleanup |
| -------- | --------- | --------- | -------- | ------- |
| Marketing header/footer | `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl` | delegate | delegate | `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl` only |
| PCMS-003 doc | `/me/registrations` hardcoded | delegation | updated text | updated text |
| Workspace registration CTA | hardcoded `href="/me/..."` | injected `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(host)` | same | same |
| GSH unit tests | `/me/registrations` | delegation + module URL tests | + module id tests | remove deprecated tests |
| SMK-PTL-05 | `/` → `/me/registrations` | unchanged until default changes | update when default → `home` | green |
| SMK-PTL-02/04 | `/me/registrations` | **always green** | **always green** | **always green** |

---

## 6. Migration timeline

| Phase | Portal Shell | Builder work | `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl` |
| ----- | ------------ | ------------ | ---------------------------- |
| 0 | RFC merge | Contract signed (this doc) | unchanged — hardcoded |
| 1 | Portal shell | none | unchanged |
| 2 | Member registry | codegen produces `defaultPrimaryModuleId` | unchanged |
| **3** | URL builder | **Implement** `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl`; delegate deprecated API | **delegate** |
| 4 | Member home | default may become `home`; alias `/me/registrations` retained | delegate |
| 5 | Entitlements | module-scoped URLs | delegate |
| 6 | Telegram adapter | uses module URL builder | delegate |
| 7 | Scale | no builder change | delegate |
| **8** | **Cleanup** | remove deprecated export; update all call sites | **removed** |

---

## 7. Deprecation strategy

1. **Phase 3:** Add `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl`; change `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl` body to delegate; add `@deprecated` JSDoc; extend GSH tests.
2. **Phase 3–7:** `guard-member-url-builder` warns on new call sites importing deprecated symbol (see [guard-member-portal-registry.md](../../dev/guard-member-portal-registry.md)).
3. **Cleanup Phase:** Remove export; CI fail on any import of `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl`; update PCMS-003, marketing, tests.

**No breaking removal** before Cleanup Phase gate green.

---

## 8. Smoke-test compatibility

| Smoke | Must pass when | Assertion |
| ----- | -------------- | --------- |
| SMK-PTL-02 | Always | List at `/me/registrations` |
| SMK-PTL-04 | Always | Detail under `/me/registrations/{id}` |
| SMK-PTL-05 | Phase 1–3 | `/` → `/me/registrations` |
| SMK-PTL-05 | Phase 4+ (when default → `home`) | `/` → `/me/home` — **explicit smoke update PR** |
| SMK-PTL-06 | Always | Logout unchanged |
| SMK-PTL-07/08 | Always | Host bind unchanged |
| GSH unit spec | Phase 3+ | `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl(h) === resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl(h)` |

**Rule:** No Phase 3 GSH PR merges unless SMK-PTL-02/04/06/07/08 green **and** delegation unit test green.

---

## 9. Backwards compatibility guarantees

| Guarantee | Duration |
| --------- | -------- |
| `/me/registrations` URL valid | Permanent (URL freeze) |
| `resolvePortalMemberAreaUrl` exported | Phase 3 through Phase 7 |
| Delegation equivalence | Phase 3 through Phase 7 |
| Hardcoded `/me/registrations` in GSH | Until Phase 3 PR merges |
| Marketing can use deprecated API | Until Cleanup Phase |

